WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.403
-Our first guest tonight is
an Emmy Award-winning actor

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:04.704
you know from
his work on "Mad Men"

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:06.839
and movies such as "The Town"
and "Baby Driver."

00:00:06.839 --> 00:00:10.376
He stars alongside Tom Cruise
in "Top Gun: Maverick,"

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:12.178
which opens
in theaters May 27th.

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:13.413
Let's take a look.

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:19.719
-Captain Pete
"Maverick" Mitchell.

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:21.654
Your reputation precedes you.

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:23.989
-Thank you, sir.

00:00:23.989 --> 00:00:26.693
-Wasn't a compliment.

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:29.562
I'm Admiral Beau Simpson.

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:30.663
I'm the air boss.

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:31.831
I believe you know
Admiral Bates.

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:33.499
-Warlock, sir.

00:00:33.499 --> 00:00:36.235
I must admit, I wasn't expecting
an invitation back.

00:00:36.235 --> 00:00:38.204
-They're called orders,
Maverick.

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:40.907
You two have
something in common.

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:43.809
Cyclone here was
first in his class back in '88.

00:00:43.809 --> 00:00:46.446
-Actually, sir,
I finished second.

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:48.648
Just want to
manage the expectations.

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:53.119
-Please welcome back to the show
our good friend Jon Hamm!

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:55.355
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:01:07.533 --> 00:01:09.802
Hi!
-Howdy!

00:01:09.802 --> 00:01:12.472
-It has -- It's been forever.
It's really been forever.

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:14.540
I used to see you all the time,
and then the last time

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:16.676
you were here was for the finale
of "Mad Men," in 2015,

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:17.677
which is nuts.

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:18.912
-Seven years ago.
-Seven years ago.

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:20.379
-Yeah, and nothing has
happened since then.

00:01:20.379 --> 00:01:21.747
-Nothing has happened
since then.

00:01:21.747 --> 00:01:23.916
That's the thing --
we would've brought you back,

00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:25.351
but the world is
absolutely the same.

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:27.887
So, you -- Well, before we
talk about "Top Bun: Maverick,"

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:30.256
which I'm so excited about,
Alexi and I --

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:31.524
we rewatched "Mad Men."

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:33.226
I feel like that was
one of those pandemic shows.

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:34.294
Did you hear from
a lot of people?

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:36.496
-I got a lot of
nice texts of like,

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:38.798
"Hey, finally got around to
watching your show."

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:41.634
I was like, "It only took
a global pandemic?"

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:42.668
Like, "Nice. Okay. Thanks."

00:01:42.668 --> 00:01:44.436
-And they were like,
"Also in 2021.

00:01:44.436 --> 00:01:45.671
We made it through the first --

00:01:45.671 --> 00:01:47.373
the first year of the pandemic,
we didn't do it."

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:48.575
-Did not.

00:01:48.575 --> 00:01:50.109
Well, they had
to get through "Sopranos"

00:01:50.109 --> 00:01:52.044
and "Breaking Bad"
and then "The Wire."

00:01:52.044 --> 00:01:55.347
But, no, it was always
a pleasant thing

00:01:55.347 --> 00:01:58.217
to get when somebody says like,
"Oh, I really like your work."

00:01:58.217 --> 00:02:00.820
-And I will say,
it holds up so well.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.188
Like, I mean,
I think it's any --

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:04.824
Like, period things
have this ability to hold up

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:06.826
because it was already -- It
took place in a different time.

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:09.395
-Yeah, in a
different world anyway.

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:12.398
So it's -- But, yeah, you know,
I'm very proud of that show.

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:15.101
It was -- I worked on it
for the better part of a decade.

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:17.237
-Yeah. And Alexi and I
loved watching it together.

00:02:17.237 --> 00:02:19.371
It's such a beautiful show
about marriage.

00:02:19.371 --> 00:02:21.441
-Yeah, really, really...

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:23.309
-Everything it says
is so wonderful.

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:24.877
-...brings couples together.

00:02:24.877 --> 00:02:26.613
-So, we were talking backstage.

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:29.315
We are of a similar age,
where the first "Top Gun"

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:31.584
was a formative film,
a seminal film.

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:34.219
-A seminal experience,
not just a film.

00:02:34.219 --> 00:02:36.856
-Right. Going to see it
in the theaters was a huge deal.

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:39.893
-I've described it as like
the definition of cool.

00:02:39.893 --> 00:02:42.395
For 15-year-old me in
the Midwest --

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:44.797
and I'm sure for you
in the Northeast, as well --

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:46.064
it was just like,
"Well, that's --

00:02:46.064 --> 00:02:47.599
Oh, that's what cool is."

00:02:47.599 --> 00:02:51.404
Sunglasses, volleyball,
aircraft.

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:53.873
-Yeah, everything.
-You know, those three things.

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:55.708
-Yeah.

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:56.809
A lot of people are like, "Wait.

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:58.177
That was what
was cool in the '80s?"

00:02:58.177 --> 00:02:59.778
-Yeah! Sunglasses, volleyball --

00:02:59.778 --> 00:03:03.215
-Yeah, and two out of three
of them still are!

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:05.384
I'm not gonna say which.

00:03:05.384 --> 00:03:07.387
-Volley and ball.

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:10.055
I feel like there were
a lot of volleyball movies

00:03:10.055 --> 00:03:11.190
in the '80s, though.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:12.325
-There were.
-Right?

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:15.128
-"Side Out," anybody?
And that's it.

00:03:15.128 --> 00:03:17.629
-Yeah, "Side Out."

00:03:17.629 --> 00:03:20.700
The other crazy thing about this
movie is it was --

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.202
You filmed
"Top Gun: Maverick" in --

00:03:23.202 --> 00:03:25.838
-2018 and 2019.
-So that's a long time ago.

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:27.840
-A long time ago.
And then it sat.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.675
It was meant to
come out in 2020,

00:03:29.675 --> 00:03:31.710
and then the world
had different plans.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:35.114
And we had to sit on it
for two years, basically,

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:37.216
and no one could see it.

00:03:37.216 --> 00:03:40.219
-And sit on it because
there was a real sense that

00:03:40.219 --> 00:03:41.754
it was going to be important
to see this in theaters.

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:43.723
-In theaters.
Yeah, big and loud.

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:46.826
That was a Tom Cruise mandate,
which we were

00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:49.462
very happy to support,
because it was --

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:52.164
It really does play as
a theatrical,

00:03:52.164 --> 00:03:53.432
as I said, experience.

00:03:53.432 --> 00:03:55.067
Like, you feel this movie,

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:56.268
like, right in the chest.

00:03:56.268 --> 00:03:57.804
It's amazing.
-We saw a little in the clip.

00:03:57.804 --> 00:03:59.772
You kind of get to be a thing
that I don't think

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:01.173
a lot of people
in real life get to be,

00:04:01.173 --> 00:04:02.341
which is a little bit mean
to Tom Cruise.

00:04:02.341 --> 00:04:03.342
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:03.342 --> 00:04:04.510
-A little bit.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:05.912
-I don't think anybody
talks to him

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:07.780
the way you talked to him
in that clip.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:09.348
-No.
-Yeah.

00:04:09.348 --> 00:04:10.950
-The fun thing is
that it's scripted.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:12.385
-Yeah.

00:04:12.385 --> 00:04:15.121
-And believe it or not, he might
get the upper hand in the end.

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:16.255
-Yeah, yeah. He might.
-Come on.

00:04:16.255 --> 00:04:17.523
-You know what?

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:18.791
I think he even knew
in that clip he might, yeah.

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:19.992
-It seemed like he did.

00:04:19.992 --> 00:04:22.361
He was like, "I read
the rest of this scene,

00:04:22.361 --> 00:04:23.929
and I'm going to be okay."

00:04:23.929 --> 00:04:25.364
-This isn't my first
Tom Cruise movie.

00:04:25.364 --> 00:04:26.832
I think I know how this ends.

00:04:26.832 --> 00:04:29.101
You know,
I've heard a lot of interviews,

00:04:29.101 --> 00:04:31.036
a lot of the cast.

00:04:31.036 --> 00:04:33.272
You do not play one of the
pilots who flies.

00:04:33.272 --> 00:04:34.807
-No.
-Who all did flight training?

00:04:34.807 --> 00:04:36.642
Did you ever feel like you were
missing out on an element of --

00:04:36.642 --> 00:04:40.412
-They had to do
4 1/2 months -- months --

00:04:40.412 --> 00:04:42.115
of preparation and training
for that,

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:45.050
some 60 hours
of being in a cockpit.

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:47.152
And being in a cockpit
is not comfortable

00:04:47.152 --> 00:04:49.355
in the best-case scenario.

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:52.291
It's really not comfortable when
you're covered in your own vomit

00:04:52.291 --> 00:04:54.960
and going around and around
and pulling all the G's

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:57.229
and all the blood's
leaving your head.

00:04:57.229 --> 00:05:01.600
So, I was very happy to leave
my shoes on the ground.

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:05.170
And I got to go on
an active aircraft carrier,

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:08.574
the USS Theodore Roosevelt,
"America's Big Stick."

00:05:08.574 --> 00:05:12.077
It's literally --
It says it on there.

00:05:12.077 --> 00:05:13.613
-Yeah, that's great.
-You can't make that up.

00:05:13.613 --> 00:05:15.314
-No, that's great.

00:05:15.314 --> 00:05:18.217
-And it was impressive.
It was impressive.

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:22.955
It was impressive to see
the scope of all of that,

00:05:22.955 --> 00:05:24.924
but also just the --
what the men and women

00:05:24.924 --> 00:05:26.858
in the U.S. Armed Services,
especially the Navy,

00:05:26.858 --> 00:05:28.627
go through
and sacrifice every day.

00:05:28.627 --> 00:05:31.864
It was a real impressive thing
to see firsthand.

00:05:31.864 --> 00:05:34.166
-Yeah, I think we all see it
often in a wide shot,

00:05:34.166 --> 00:05:35.734
and it must have been
really cool to be up close.

00:05:35.734 --> 00:05:36.802
-Yeah, and terrifying,
by the way,

00:05:36.802 --> 00:05:38.571
because you realize
you're on a boat

00:05:38.571 --> 00:05:41.407
that has two working
nuclear reactors on it.

00:05:41.407 --> 00:05:43.442
And so you're like,
"What does this button do?"

00:05:43.442 --> 00:05:45.811
"No, no, no, no!"

00:05:45.811 --> 00:05:47.412
-They shouldn't --
That button shouldn't be out.

00:05:47.412 --> 00:05:48.514
-It shouldn't be out.

00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:49.515
-It shouldn't be out in the room

00:05:49.515 --> 00:05:50.749
where they bring
the actors into.

00:05:50.749 --> 00:05:52.184
-There should at least be,
like, a weird cover

00:05:52.184 --> 00:05:53.953
that you have to flip over it.

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:56.355
-There's also a -- There is
a volleyball scene --

00:05:56.355 --> 00:05:57.757
-Volleyball adjacent.
-Volleyball adjacent.

00:05:57.757 --> 00:05:59.058
-Yes.

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:01.761
-You were not -- But shirts --
A lot of shirts off.

00:06:01.761 --> 00:06:03.363
-A lot of shirts off.
Not this guy.

00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:05.197
-Not this guy, yeah.
Very well done.

00:06:05.197 --> 00:06:08.434
-This is what 51 years on
the planet teaches you.

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:11.770
-They're like, "We're going to
get you in the boardroom."

00:06:11.770 --> 00:06:13.305
-Yeah, exactly.

00:06:13.305 --> 00:06:17.410
Tie, button it up,
you know, shiny shoes.

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:20.012
-But that -- I mean, talk about
4 1/2 months in a cockpit.

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:22.548
I saw shots of those guys.
That'd be like 4 1/2 years.

00:06:22.548 --> 00:06:24.450
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:30.456
-The topless scene -- "Topless."
That sounds weird already.

00:06:30.456 --> 00:06:34.259
But the football, volleyball,
the sports scene --

00:06:34.259 --> 00:06:37.696
-Yeah. Yeah.
It's about sports, you guys!

00:06:37.696 --> 00:06:39.165
-Beach sports.

00:06:39.165 --> 00:06:41.366
-Beach sports, okay?
Get your head out of the gutter.

00:06:41.366 --> 00:06:43.336
-Yeah, come on.

00:06:43.336 --> 00:06:45.338
I not only left my shirt on,

00:06:45.338 --> 00:06:48.741
I have loafers and socks on
on the beach.

00:06:48.741 --> 00:06:51.377
So I am full granddadding it.

00:06:51.377 --> 00:06:53.479
-We saw it a little bit there.

00:06:53.479 --> 00:06:55.814
As call signs go, I remember
that was the thing.

00:06:55.814 --> 00:06:59.618
When we talked out of "Top Gun"
when it came out --

00:06:59.618 --> 00:07:01.787
-Maverick, Goose,
Slider, Jester.

00:07:01.787 --> 00:07:02.955
-Jester, yeah.

00:07:02.955 --> 00:07:04.256
-Yeah, it was amazing.
Everyone had a cool one.

00:07:04.256 --> 00:07:05.490
-And you got a good one,
"Cyclone."

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:07.660
-I got a good one. Cyclone.
-Cyclone is great.

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:10.162
-Cyclone is good. It's an emoji.

00:07:10.162 --> 00:07:11.363
-Yeah.
-That works.

00:07:11.363 --> 00:07:12.932
-Yeah.
-There's no Maverick emoji.

00:07:12.932 --> 00:07:15.634
-There's no Maverick, yeah.

00:07:15.634 --> 00:07:17.503
By the way, I get a sense
if Tom Cruise hears that,

00:07:17.503 --> 00:07:18.537
there just might be.

00:07:18.537 --> 00:07:20.673
-There's gonna be
a Maverick tomorrow.

00:07:20.673 --> 00:07:23.376
-And, also, like,
it's just gonna be him.

00:07:24.777 --> 00:07:26.011
-Yeah, I wouldn't
put it past him.

00:07:26.011 --> 00:07:27.412
-Yeah, I thought a lot
personally about, like,

00:07:27.412 --> 00:07:28.714
if I -- What would --

00:07:28.714 --> 00:07:31.850
-I bet you -- I could come up
with a couple good ones.

00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:33.986
Right out of the gate, Frisbee.

00:07:33.986 --> 00:07:35.721
-Frisbee as a call sign?
-Yeah, Frisbee.

00:07:35.721 --> 00:07:37.055
-I don't know -- Frisbee's okay.

00:07:37.055 --> 00:07:38.391
I think Frisbee shows,
like, yeah,

00:07:38.391 --> 00:07:40.759
there's something fun
about Frisbee.

00:07:40.759 --> 00:07:43.696
-It's a beach sport.
-Yeah, it's a beach sport.

00:07:43.696 --> 00:07:45.364
It's a beach sport they say --
It's weird.

00:07:45.364 --> 00:07:47.400
They say,
"Keep your T-shirt on."

00:07:48.567 --> 00:07:49.735
-Doink.
-Doink.

00:07:49.735 --> 00:07:50.970
-Doink would be
a good one for you.

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:52.838
-I don't know if Doink --
I feel less, like --

00:07:52.838 --> 00:07:55.808
I would feel bad making
my colleagues have to say,

00:07:55.808 --> 00:07:56.875
"Cover me, Doink."

00:07:56.875 --> 00:07:58.478
-Cover me, Doink.

00:08:00.112 --> 00:08:02.214
Although, if you ever went down,
"My Doink fell off" would --

00:08:02.214 --> 00:08:04.817
-Yeah, my Doink fell down.
Doink is down!

00:08:04.817 --> 00:08:06.752
-We got Doink down.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.888
-Anything else? What else?

00:08:09.888 --> 00:08:10.889
I'm gonna pick one.
-Alright, you go.

00:08:10.889 --> 00:08:11.957
-I will pick one.
You got some?

00:08:11.957 --> 00:08:13.325
-I've got a bunch.
-Okay, great.

00:08:13.325 --> 00:08:15.427
-I actually -- I told your
writers to come up with a bunch.

00:08:15.427 --> 00:08:16.929
-Oh, no.

00:08:19.198 --> 00:08:20.766
-Oh, there's a list.
-Okay, great.

00:08:20.766 --> 00:08:24.936
-Cyclone's Friend.
-Okay.

00:08:24.936 --> 00:08:27.540
I don't hate it.
I don't hate it.

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:29.641
-B.J. Novak.

00:08:29.641 --> 00:08:31.844
-That's not a call sign!

00:08:31.844 --> 00:08:34.347
You can't say B.J. --
Yeah, okay.

00:08:36.014 --> 00:08:37.583
-Sea Captain.
-Okay, Sea Captain.

00:08:37.583 --> 00:08:39.919
I don't mind -- See, I mean,
it's a little counterintuitive

00:08:39.919 --> 00:08:41.153
when you're in the sky.

00:08:41.153 --> 00:08:42.555
-True.

00:08:44.023 --> 00:08:46.725
And then Stewardess.
-Stewardess?

00:08:47.159 --> 00:08:49.161
I'm going Frisbee.
I'm going Frisbee.

00:08:49.161 --> 00:08:50.162
-Thank you. Thank you very much.
-Alright.

00:08:50.162 --> 00:08:51.998
You guys, that's Jon Hamm.

00:08:51.998 --> 00:08:53.799
"Top Gun: Maverick"
is in theaters Friday.

00:08:53.799 --> 00:08:55.401
We'll be right back with
Julio Torres.

